    body: `<h2>Territorial Jurisdiction of Family Courts</h2><p>Under Section 19 of the Hindu Marriage Act, a petition for divorce or matrimonial relief must be filed in the Family Court within whose local limits:</p><ul><li>The marriage was solemnised;</li><li>The respondent resides at the time of filing;</li><li>The parties to the marriage last resided together; or</li><li>The wife resides on the date of presentation of the petition (where she is the petitioner).</li></ul><h2>Procedural Hierarchy of Matrimonial Proceedings</h2><p>Family Courts follow a structured procedural path combining Civil Procedure Code principles with mandatory conciliation obligations under Section 9 of the Family Courts Act, 1984.</p>`
